{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>About, attribution &amp; privacy</h1>

<h2>What this is</h2>
<p>
  A free, static mirror of the California Department of Fish and Wildlife's
  weekly trout (and occasional catfish) planting schedule, organised by
  water, with the full planting history this site has observed &mdash; CDFW's
  own page shows a rolling window of about a year, and this site keeps every
  week it has recorded after that window moves on.
</p>

<h2 id="privacy">Privacy: literally nothing is collected</h2>
<p>This is a plain static site. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
  <li>No cookies are set by this site.</li>
  <li>No JavaScript runs on this site, at all &mdash; there is nothing to run
      analytics, tracking, or a "third-party script" with.</li>
  <li>No request made by a page on this site contacts any server other than
      the one serving the page itself. Nothing you do here leaves your
      browser.</li>
  <li>No account, no email address, no sign-up, anywhere on this site.</li>
  <li>Calendar subscriptions (.ics) are plain files; your calendar app
      fetches them directly from this site on whatever schedule it chooses.
      This site does not know who has subscribed.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Standard web server logs (IP address, requested path, timestamp) are kept
  by GitHub Pages, which hosts this site &mdash; see GitHub's own
  <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy
  statement</a>. This site does not add any collection on top of that.
</p>

<h2 id="app">The iOS app</h2>
<p>
  A companion iOS app lets you favourite waters and browse the same planting
  history as this site, free. A one-time in-app purchase &mdash; not a
  subscription &mdash; adds a local notification when a favourite appears in
  a new week's schedule. The notification is generated on your device from a
  snapshot the app downloads periodically in the background &mdash; there is
  no push service, no account, and no server that knows which waters you
  favourited. The schedule updates weekly, so alerts arrive on CDFW's
  schedule, not instantly.
</p>
{% if app_store_url %}
<p><a href="{{ app_store_url }}">Get the app on the App Store</a>.</p>
{% else %}
<p>The app is not in the App Store yet; this page will link to it once it is.</p>
{% endif %}
<p>Details: <a href="{{ root }}privacy/">privacy policy</a> &middot; <a href="{{ root }}support/">support &amp; FAQ</a>.</p>

<h2>Data, licence &amp; attribution</h2>
<p>{{ attribution_text }}</p>
<p>{{ licence_summary }}</p>
<table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Sources this site is built from, with licence terms</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Source</th>
      <th scope="col">Terms read on</th>
      <th scope="col">Commercial reuse</th>
      <th scope="col">Attribution required</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for s in licence_sources %}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{ s.url }}">{{ s.name }}</a></td>
      <td>{{ s.terms_read_on }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.commercial_reuse }}</td>
      <td>{{ "yes" if s.attribution_required else "no" }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Accuracy</h2>
<p>
  CDFW: "all fish plants are subject to change depending on road, water,
  weather and operational conditions." Every date on this site is a
  <strong>week</strong>, never a day &mdash; CDFW does not publish a more
  specific date, on purpose ("to avoid focusing excess fishing activity
  immediately after a plant"). Nothing on this site should be read as
  confirmation that a plant happened.
</p>

<h2>Source</h2>
<p>
  Generated {{ generated_at_label }} from
  <a href="{{ attribution_url }}">CDFW's Fish Planting Schedule</a>, fetched
  {{ source_fetched_label }}. Machine-readable snapshot:
  <a href="{{ root }}snapshot/v1.json">{{ root }}snapshot/v1.json</a>.
</p>
{% endblock %}
